orld's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2022, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2022, "rank": 211, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2021, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2021, "rank": 188, "itemDescription": "Founded as a small soap and candle business in 1806, the consumer products company now boasts a portfolio of well-known household and personal care brands."}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2020, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2020, "rank": 203, "itemDescription": "Colgate-Palmolive's diverse portfolio of home, personal, and oral care brands\u2014which includes names like Ajax, Irish Spring, and Speedstick\u2014are sold in more than 200 countries and territories."}, {"slug": "change-the-world", "title": "Change the World", "year": 2020, "rank": 27, "itemDescription": "Toothpaste tubes have long frustrated green-minded consumers. The hybrid composition that makes such tubes squeezable\u2014a mixture of laminated plastic and aluminum\u2014also makes it impracticable to recycle most of the 20 billion tubes that consumers discard each year.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nColgate-Palmolive, which claims 41% of the global toothpaste market, poured five years of research into this puzzle, and in 2019, the effort paid off. Colgate\u2019s new recyclable tube is made from high-density polyethylene (HDPE), the recyclable plastic found in shampoo containers and milk jugs. (A key phase of the research: grinding down the tube prototypes and recycling them as new bottles.) This year, Colgate introduced the tubes in multiple brands and it will soon use them for Optic White, which alone accounts for 8.5% of U.S. toothpaste sales. The company aims to make 100% of its packaging recyclable by 2025. In the meantime, it\u2019s sharing the HDPE design on an open-source basis, so others can adopt it too."}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2019, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2019, "rank": 202, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2018, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2018, "rank": 184, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2017, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2017, "rank": 182, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2016, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2016, "rank": 174, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2015, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2015, "rank": 179, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2014, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2014, "rank": 167, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2013, "rank": 165, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2012, "rank": 155, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2011, "rank": 160, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2010, "rank": 151, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2009, "